ASSIGNMENT 2
Create and Deploy a Wave Smart Contract Using Remix IDE and Connect with MetaMask
========================================

1. Open Remix IDE:
https://remix.ethereum.org

2. Create a Solidity file named:
WavePortal.sol

3. Write the following Solidity code:

// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
pragma solidity ^0.8.0;

contract WavePortal {

    uint public totalWaves;

    struct Wave {
        address waver;
        string message;
        uint timestamp;
    }

    Wave[] public waves;

    function wave(string memory _message) public {

        totalWaves += 1;

        waves.push(
            Wave(
                msg.sender,
                _message,
                block.timestamp
            )
        );
    }

    function getAllWaves() public view returns (Wave[] memory) {
        return waves;
    }

    function getTotalWaves() public view returns (uint) {
        return totalWaves;
    }
}

4. Open Solidity Compiler tab.

5. Compile WavePortal.sol.

6. Open Deploy & Run Transactions tab.

7. Select Environment:
Remix VM

8. Select contract:
WavePortal

9. Click Deploy.

10. Test functions:
- wave()
- getAllWaves()
- getTotalWaves()

11. Open MetaMask and switch to Sepolia network.

12. Ensure Sepolia ETH is available in wallet.

13. In Remix change Environment to:
Injected Provider - MetaMask

14. Connect MetaMask wallet.

15. Click Deploy.

16. Confirm deployment transaction in MetaMask.

17. Check contract deployment in MetaMask Activity tab.

18. Test contract functions again.
